uper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-13T23:21:21Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T23:21:21Z","body":"PR rebased, LGTM","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6157284363/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6162834144","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112098#issuecomment-6162834144","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112098","id":6162834144,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABb1Vi4A","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-14T07:02:43Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T11:20:17Z","body":"This will fail with long thin triangles, and also requires user involvement.\r\n\r\nHow about this instead:\r\n* for each mesh, calculate the maximum side length of triangles (ahead of time, e.g. at import)\r\n* add THIS to the radius of the light in order to decide whether to cull\r\n\r\nYou can use this in combination with tessellating meshes (to limit long thin triangles), even at the art stage, to make this work efficiently and robustly.\r\n\r\nThis won't be perfect with skinned meshes, that might need some fudge factor.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6162834144/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6176195636","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112098#issuecomment-6176195636","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112098","id":6176195636,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcCFENA","user":{"login":"ghostsoft","id":63552156,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTUyMTU2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63552156?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft","html_url":"https://github.com/ghostsoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-14T19:09:11Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T19:10:41Z","body":"> This will fail with long thin triangles, and also requires user involvement.\r\n\r\nThat's a strange statement. Can you elaborate on how it fails? Rather, how do you think *this PR* fails on long thin triangles? The culling as it currently works does indeed fail with long thin triangles that are vertex lit which is exactly what this PR sets out to solve and yes it requires user involvement to set the extra cull margin far enough that it encompasses all vertices of the surrounding triangles explicitly to stop the culling from kicking in too soon while the triangle is still being lit.\r\n\r\n> How about this instead:\r\n> \r\n>     * for each mesh, calculate the maximum side length of triangles (ahead of time, e.g. at import)\r\n> \r\n>     * add THIS to the radius of the light in order to decide whether to cull\r\n\r\nThis is something I've already discussed in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105063 and it's not something that's possible without a complete overhaul of how the rendering pipeline in Godot works. The lights have no knowledge of the geometry they're lighting and as such there is no way to inject that kind of data into the light's cull margin. It also would not be possible to do this at import time as the relevant factor here isn't the edge length, it's the distance of the vertex from the light (which obviously changes depending on where the light is placed and how the mesh is rotated relative to the light.) Even if this _was_ feasible, it would also overreach and bog down performance in any scene that isn't vertex lit as the lights _also_ have no way of knowing whether the materials of the meshes it lights up are pixel or vertex lit and this kind of extra cull margin is only needed for vertex lighting specifically. It's an idealistic idea that I've already humored but it would require a much deeper coupling of the lights and meshes/materials in a way that is completely incompatible with how the Godot engine is built.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6176195636/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6177273465","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112098#issuecomment-6177273465","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112098","id":6177273465,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcDG2eQ","user":{"login":"elvisish","id":16231628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjMxNjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16231628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish","html_url":"https://github.com/elvisish","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-14T20:06:03Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T20:06:03Z","body":"> and also requires user involvement.\n\nTechnically, so does extra_cull_margin in the geometry node:\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f66a7f80-4fd9-40fd-8e6b-df60dd293dc7)","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6177273465/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6184805194","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112098#issuecomment-6184805194","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112098","id":6184805194,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcKSjSg","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T05:01:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T05:16:49Z","body":"> This will fail with long thin triangles, and also requires user involvement.\r\n\r\nYup sure - as I understand it, long thin triangles is the Achilles heel of vertex lighting, because it has to interpolate across the triangle.\r\n\r\nIf any one of the verts of a triangle is in a light, the whole triangle (and likely the mesh) has to be rendered as \"light aware\". i.e. if you are looking at one side of a map, if a single triangle in your view frustum has a corner a mile away next to a light, then that light needs to be used in rendering the mesh (even though it is a mile away).\r\n\r\nSo if you have e.g. a landscape that is mostly tessellated, but contains a few long thin triangles, you can't tune the cull margin to the average case, you have to tune it to the _worst_ case (which is the long thin triangles). This is hard to do exhaustively as a user.\r\n\r\n## The fundamental thing this PR does wrong\r\nI've realised the main mistake this PR makes is it is adding this cull margin to the _light_, but it should be stored per _mesh_. The _mesh_ determines the cull margin, via the longest edge.\r\n\r\nThus the collision check should take into account the light AABB, the mesh AABB, and the mesh cull margin (from the longest edge of the mesh triangles).\r\n\r\n## Other problems\r\nWhile it might be quick to guesstimate a cull margin for a simple mesh, on complex meshes, it is very hard to be exhaustive about the max length of the triangles (different light / mesh angles etc), coupled with the problem that every time you edit a model in blender and re-export, this cull margin may change.\r\n\r\nThis is lending itself to an automated approach.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6184805194/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6186502209","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112098#issuecomment-6186502209","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112098","id":6186502209,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcL6IQQ","user":{"login":"ghostsoft","id":63552156,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTUyMTU2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63552156?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft","html_url":"https://github.com/ghostsoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T07:05:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T07:05:26Z","body":"I think you're confused, the individual mesh has no say in how and when each light is culled. This is not something that happens \"per mesh\", it's something that's happening to the light itself when the light is far enough outside the camera frustum to be considered by the engine \"no longer in view\". This PR lets the user extend how far the light can be outside of view while still not being culled by the engine's culling code. Your solution here is completely nonsensical and quite confusing... you mention a collision check but there is no such thing happening at any point here. The light is simply a data structure passed to the shader.\r\n\r\nAs for the long, thin triangles I am very aware of that as I have talked about this plenty in the issue I linked in my previous post which also includes diagrams and screenshots/clips to show in full how this problem occurs and why this PR lets the user fix those problems specifically for cases where there are long thin triangles or otherwise vertices outside of the reach of the light itself, \"stretching\" the lit area further than the light's radius. I am very well aware of how vertex lighting works.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6186502209/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6338493616","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112098#issuecomment-6338493616","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112098","id":6338493616,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABec28sA","user":{"login":"ghostsoft","id":63552156,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTUyMTU2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63552156?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft","html_url":"https://github.com/ghostsoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-22T10:25:28Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T10:25:28Z","body":"The suggested changes have been added and the PR has been squashed to a single commit. That should leave it in a pretty pristine state for merging I think!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6338493616/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]